{"cells": [{"cell_type": "markdown", "id": "799fdac1", "metadata": {}, "source": ["# Sales analysis - a RAD IDE notebook\n", "(c) 2026 Musoftware - https://musoftwares.com - MIT License\n", "\n", "This notebook reads `sales.csv` (next to it) and answers a few questions with the **Python standard library only**\n", "(no pandas needed): totals per region and product, the best month, a month-over-month trend and a text bar chart.\n", "\n", "*\u062a\u062d\u0644\u064a\u0644 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0628\u064a\u0639\u0627\u062a - \u062f\u0641\u062a\u0631 Jupyter \u0641\u064a RAD IDE: \u064a\u0642\u0631\u0623 \u0645\u0644\u0641 sales.csv \u0648\u064a\u062d\u0633\u0628 \u0627\u0644\u0625\u062c\u0645\u0627\u0644\u064a\u0627\u062a \u062d\u0633\u0628 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0646\u0637\u0642\u0629 \u0648\u0627\u0644\u0645\u0646\u062a\u062c \u0648\u0623\u0641\u0636\u0644 \u0634\u0647\u0631 \u0648\u0627\u062a\u062c\u0627\u0647 \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0628\u064a\u0639\u0627\u062a\u060c \u0628\u0627\u0633\u062a\u062e\u062f\u0627\u0645 \u0645\u0643\u062a\u0628\u0629 \u0628\u0627\u064a\u062b\u0648\u0646 \u0627\u0644\u0642\u064a\u0627\u0633\u064a\u0629 \u0641\u0642\u0637.*\n", "\n", "Run the cells from top to bottom (Shift+Enter) or **Run All**."]}, {"cell_type": "code", "id": "00f1b0de", "metadata": {}, "source": ["# (c) 2026 Musoftware - https://musoftwares.com - MIT License\n", "import csv\n", "import statistics\n", "from collections import defaultdict\n", "from pathlib import Path\n", "\n", "rows = []\n", "with open(Path(\"sales.csv\"), encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n", "    for r in csv.DictReader(f):\n", "        r[\"Units\"] = int(r[\"Units\"])\n", "        r[\"Price\"] = float(r[\"Price\"])\n", "        r[\"Revenue\"] = r[\"Units\"] * r[\"Price\"]\n", "        rows.append(r)\n", "print(len(rows), \"rows,\", len({r['Month'] for r in rows}), \"months\")"], "execution_count": null, "outputs": []}, {"cell_type": "markdown", "id": "7b51308f", "metadata": {}, "source": ["## Revenue per region and per product"]}, {"cell_type": "code", "id": "755dbcc6", "metadata": {}, "source": ["def total_by(key):\n", "    out = defaultdict(float)\n", "    for r in rows:\n", "        out[r[key]] += r[\"Revenue\"]\n", "    return dict(sorted(out.items(), key=lambda kv: -kv[1]))\n", "\n", "by_region = total_by(\"Region\")\n", "by_product = total_by(\"Product\")\n", "for name, value in by_region.items():\n", "    print(f\"{name:<12}{value:>10,.2f}\")\n", "print()\n", "for name, value in by_product.items():\n", "    print(f\"{name:<12}{value:>10,.2f}\")"], "execution_count": null, "outputs": []}, {"cell_type": "markdown", "id": "dabab3ba", "metadata": {}, "source": ["## Best month and month-over-month change"]}, {"cell_type": "code", "id": "c1c14b0b", "metadata": {}, "source": ["by_month = dict(sorted(total_by(\"Month\").items()))\n", "best = max(by_month, key=by_month.get)\n", "print(\"best month:\", best, f\"{by_month[best]:,.2f}\")\n", "months = list(by_month)\n", "for prev, cur in zip(months, months[1:]):\n", "    change = (by_month[cur] - by_month[prev]) / by_month[prev] * 100\n", "    print(f\"{cur}: {by_month[cur]:>9,.2f}  ({change:+.1f} %)\")\n", "print(\"average month:\", f\"{statistics.mean(by_month.values()):,.2f}\",\n", "      \" stdev:\", f\"{statistics.stdev(by_month.values()):,.2f}\")"], "execution_count": null, "outputs": []}, {"cell_type": "markdown", "id": "82ecdd8e", "metadata": {}, "source": ["## A text bar chart\n", "Every `#` is about 2 % of the best month."]}, {"cell_type": "code", "id": "d7a0ec31", "metadata": {}, "source": ["top = max(by_month.values())\n", "for month, value in by_month.items():\n", "    print(f\"{month}  {'#' * round(value / top * 50):<50}  {value:,.0f}\")"], "execution_count": null, "outputs": []}, {"cell_type": "markdown", "id": "f34583fd", "metadata": {}, "source": ["## Your turn\n", "Change `key` to `\"Product\"` or `\"Region\"` and run the cell again."]}, {"cell_type": "code", "id": "56d25ffa", "metadata": {}, "source": true, "execution_count": null, "outputs": []}], "metadata": {"kernelspec": {"name": "python3", "display_name": "Python 3 (ipykernel)", "language": "python"}, "language_info": {"name": "python"}}, "nbformat": 4, "nbformat_minor": 5}